# git-identity: canonical identity map  (THE single source of truth)
#
# One identity per line, whitespace-separated:
#
#   <alias>   <email>               <ssh-host>
#
#   alias     short label shown in the prompt, e.g. <liotru>
#   email     the git user.email for this identity
#   ssh-host  the Host alias from ~/.ssh/config carrying this account's key
#
# The ssh-host MUST match a Host block in ~/.ssh/config, e.g.:
#
#     Host github-personal
#         HostName github.com
#         User git
#         IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_personal
#         IdentitiesOnly yes
#
# Lines starting with # are ignored. Fill in your own values below.
#
# Example (replace with your real accounts):
#   work       you@company.com        github.com
#   personal   you@personal.example   github-personal
